{
	"_about": "Spec 48 FR-48-60, FR-48-61, FR-48-62: how a draft's shop units (lib/shop-parts-read.mjs) map to the framework. An entry matches a unit when every criterion it names holds: `text` (a regex, case-insensitive, over the unit's ` | `-joined tag, words, aria label, placeholder, input type, handler and href), `tag` (the unit's tag), `parent` (the tag a text run sits in), `branch` (the unit's sc-if and sc-for conditions), `kind` (text, control, image or import). The first matching entry in file order wins, so specific entries come first. `home.settings` are an anchored regex resolved against the framework DB's attributes for `home.block` (an entry whose pattern finds no attribute is refused as stale); `valueFrom: text` writes the unit's literal words into the one setting the pattern names. `home.contains` names a block comment the part or template file must hold. `controlsOnly` surfaces take text runs only through an entry with `claimsText`.",
